From 3076ae873dcd6b520d155d2c7e29b4ae2b75765c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 19:16:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chore(brand): reconcile mobile app theme to the deeper,
 richer brand palette
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three brand color constants in mobile/lib/config/app_theme.dart are
updated to match the canonical brand book (May 2026 V2 palette). The
new values align with the deeper, richer color theme already present
in frontend/src/index.css, so mobile + web finally agree on a single
source of truth.

Before vs after:
  brandPrimary    #F26B3A → #F26B3A   (unchanged — Heritage Orange)
  brandSecondary  #6C8B74 → #436E55   (parchment sage → forest sage)
  brandAccent     #D9B88C → #F0C24D   (parchment gold → heritage gold)

The chipBackground tints (LightColors.chipBackground and
DarkColors.chipBackground) are deliberately left alone — they're
soft sage-toned wash colors that read fine against either sage
hue, and minimizing the visual diff here de-risks shipping.

Visual impact in the app:
  - Floating-action buttons + primary chips that read as sage now
    read as forest green (more grounded, less washed-out).
  - Premium tier badges and gold accents now read brighter / richer
    instead of parchment beige.
  - Heritage Orange CTAs are unchanged.

If a follow-up regression is needed, revert this commit and the app
returns to the parchment-toned palette V1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mobile/lib/config/app_theme.dart | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mobile/lib/config/app_theme.dart b/mobile/lib/config/app_theme.dart
index 95df876..b7b0fb8 100644
--- a/mobile/lib/config/app_theme.dart
+++ b/mobile/lib/config/app_theme.dart
@@ -1,9 +1,12 @@
 import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
 
-// Brand / Shared Colors
-const Color brandPrimary = Color(0xFFF26B3A); // Warm orange (CTA)
-const Color brandSecondary = Color(0xFF6C8B74); // Sage green
-const Color brandAccent = Color(0xFFD9B88C); // Gold / heritage accent
+// Brand / Shared Colors — palette V2 (May 2026)
+// Deeper, richer reconciliation of the parchment-toned originals with
+// the deeper values already in frontend/src/index.css. See the canonical
+// Legacy Table Brand Book for usage rules.
+const Color brandPrimary = Color(0xFFF26B3A); // Heritage Orange — primary CTAs
+const Color brandSecondary = Color(0xFF436E55); // Forest Sage — calm, family, growth
+const Color brandAccent = Color(0xFFF0C24D); // Heritage Gold — premium, ceremony
 
 // Light Theme Colors
 class LightColors {
